      "failingExample": "Falsifying example: test_list_is_tenant_scoped_filtered_ordered(rows=[], status_filter=None, kind_filter=None)\n\nsqlalchemy.exc.ProgrammingError: (asyncpg.exceptions.AmbiguousParameterError) could not determine data type of parameter $2\n[SQL: SELECT id, kind, status, requesting_agent_id, service_id, action, target_agent_id, share_direction, proposed_config, created_at, expires_at FROM access_requests WHERE tenant_id = $1 AND ($2 IS NULL OR status = $2) AND ($3 IS NULL OR kind = $3) ORDER BY created_at DESC, id DESC]\n[parameters: ('<tenant_uuid>', None, None)]\n\nRoot cause (service code, NOT the test): list_requests() in apps/admin-api/src/admin_api/services/access_requests.py builds `(:status IS NULL OR status = :status)` / `(:kind IS NULL OR kind = :kind)` and binds Python None for the no-filter case. Over asyncpg, a bare bind param that only ever appears untyped (compared to NULL and a text column) cannot have its type inferred, so Postgres raises AmbiguousParameterError. This fires on ANY unfiltered list call (minimal repro is rows=[], both filters None). A fix would cast the params, e.g. `(CAST(:status AS text) IS NULL OR status = CAST(:status AS text))`, but per Task 3.6 the service code must not be modified in this task.",
